{"text": "From: Annabeth Crowder <annabeth@crowderestate.example>\nTo: Whitney Tolleson <whitney.tolleson@piedmontmail.example>, Marcus Tolleson <mtolleson@uwharriefurniture.example>\nDate: Wed, 5 Nov 2025 08:41:27 -0500\nSubject: RE: beneficiary forms - please do NOT name Eli directly\n\nWhitney, Marcus,\n\nGood questions. Short answers first, then the list.\n\nPlease do not name Eli as a direct beneficiary of anything. Because he receives SSI and Medicaid, an inheritance in his own name of more than $2,000 would cut off his benefits. Everything meant for him should name \"the trustee of the Eli Tolleson Supplemental Needs Trust dated October 30, 2025.\" The trust's EIN is 39-4418772. Harper's share can go to her outright through a custodian until she is 25.\n\nWhat to change, account by account:\n\n1. Marcus's 401(k) at Uwharrie Furniture Group (plan participant ID UFG-204418, balance about $312,000): primary Whitney 100%; contingent 50% the trust, 50% Harper.\n2. Whitney's rollover IRA at Catawba Trust Bank, account CTB-7700418: same pattern.\n3. Yadkin Fidelity Life term policy no. YF-0044187-T, face amount $750,000, insured Marcus (the application shows SSN ending 6049 - please confirm that is right, I have 6094 in my notes).\n4. Joint checking and savings at Catawba: leave as they are; the wills cover them.\n\nGuardian. You named Whitney's sister, Paige Dunaway, of Greensboro. I need her date of birth and a phone number for the nomination, and she should know that Eli's guardianship continues after he turns 18; we would file for adult guardianship the year before his 18th birthday, i.e. in 2027.\n\nFee: the flat fee of $4,800 covers all of this. Balance due at signing is $2,400. Signing is Thursday, November 20 at 2:00 at our office, 301 N. Elm Street, Suite 600, Greensboro, NC 27401. Bring driver's licenses.\n\nAnnabeth\n\nAnnabeth Crowder | Crowder Estate Planning, PLLC | 336-555-0155\n\nOn Tue, Nov 4, 2025 at 9:58 PM Whitney Tolleson wrote:\n> Annabeth - Marcus's HR sent the 401k beneficiary form and it wants names + SSNs + birthdates for the kids. I was going to put:\n> Eli James Tolleson, 06/17/2010, 117-88-5665\n> Harper Tolleson, 01/09/2013, 734-02-3590\n> Is that wrong for Eli because of the trust? His SSI is $967 a month and we can't lose the Medicaid waiver, his ABA therapy and the autism day program run through it.\n> Also Paige said yes to being guardian. Her cell is 336.555.0121. She asked if her DUI from college is a problem??\n> W.", "kind": "Email", "detail": "399 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Annabeth Crowder", "Whitney Tolleson", "Marcus Tolleson", "Eli Tolleson", "Harper", "Annabeth", "Marcus", "Eli James Tolleson", "Harper Tolleson", "Paige"], "companies": ["Crowder Estate Planning, PLLC", "Crowder Estate", "Uwharrie Furniture", "Catawba Trust Bank", "Fidelity Life", "Greensboro", "HR"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Greensboro", "Catawba", "Uwharrie", "Yadkin"], "health": ["SSI", "Medicaid", "autism day program", "ABA therapy", "DUI"], "sensitive": ["EIN", "SSNs", "birthdates", "guardian"], "names": ["Annabeth", "Whitney", "Marcus", "Eli", "Harper", "Paige"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.6999999955296516, "modelMs": 24374.39999999851, "topicMs": 28412.89999999851, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 6, "end": 22, "text": "Annabeth Crowder", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Annabeth Crowder"}, {"start": 24, "end": 54, "text": "annabeth@crowderestate.example", "kind": "email", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "annabeth@crowderestate.example"}, {"start": 60, "end": 76, "text": "Whitney Tolleson", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Whi